NativeSupporterVault::withdraw
├── Given unknown/closed ID, wrong owner, early unlock or expired deadline
│   └── It leaves the original claim intact
├── Given ordinary state
│   ├── When canonical valuation is unavailable or custody is short
│   │   └── It requires recovery and cannot consume another bucket
│   ├── When entry/harvest is paused, report is old, or manager/redemption/USD oracle fails
│   │   └── It still permits usable native-token principal exits
│   ├── When healthy
│   │   └── It pays floor inverse, including the last claim, retaining carry and ceiling-reserve dust
│   ├── When impaired, including successful zero canonical value
│   │   ├── When not final
│   │   │   └── It pays floor(Q*b/B), keeping nominal remaining basis without a second loss write-down
│   │   └── When final
│   │       └── It pays all remaining accounted tokens
│   └── When ordinary payout is zero
│       └── It preserves the position for explicit recovery instead of closing it
├── Given recovery custody has been exported but no settlement is active
│   └── It cannot redeem principal
└── Given fixed funded settlement
    ├── It retains owner and original lock checks
    ├── It pays floor(N*b/B0) independently of rate or claim order, allowing explicit zero budgets
    └── It closes once; min-out, transfer failure and reentrancy revert the entire mutation
